    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**, who carry our top two efficiency scores at 83.29 and 75.10, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a prime matchup against Arrighetti (4.66 xERA), and his ability to leverage a significant dynamic platoon advantage makes him the cornerstone of our production today. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a breakout performance against Dobnak; the combination of a favorable SP_xERA and a high-leverage #2 spot in the order maximizes his potential for both counting stats and SB opportunities, which remains our primary objective in this 5x5 format.\n\nWe are keeping a close eye on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08), both of whom provide excellent value. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is particularly boosted by a +11% SP skill factor and a +10% park environment, providing a significant lift over his base projection. The most difficult benching decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who posted a solid 61.09 score. While **Nasim Nunez** offers the elite sprint speed we covet, the optimizer penalized his projected #9 spot in the lineup, ultimately preferring the higher RBI potential and efficiency of **Curtis Mead** and **Miguel Vargas**. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that several hitters, including **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Curtis Mead**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**, are currently listed with \"Lineup Pending\" status. While we have assumed optimal placements, any late-scratch or order-shift\u2014particularly for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** facing the tougher arm of Weathers (3.41 xERA)\u2014could necessitate a mid-day pivot to bench assets like **Heliot Ramos** or **Josh Jung**. We will continue to monitor the stadium reports to ensure our speed-heavy strategy remains intact throughout the evening.",
